# Logic folder – how to read it

This folder is the **design backbone** of NEXUS written before implementation. It mirrors the final project tree
(`nexus/…`). Every source file of the project has one logic document here with the same name plus `.md`.

Each logic document describes, in plain language and pseudocode:

1. **Purpose** – why the file exists.
2. **Responsibilities / state** – what it owns.
3. **Operations** – public methods with pre- and postconditions.
4. **Algorithm** – rough code / pseudocode of the important parts.
5. **Concepts** – which Software Construction concept the file demonstrates.
6. **Tests** – which test class covers it.

These documents, together with the official design documents (01–09) in the parent folder, were given to the AI
coding assistant to generate the implementation. The team then reviewed, tested and corrected the code
(see 10 – Software Testing Document and 11 – Bug Tracking and Resolution Report).

## Suggested implementation order
| Step | Files | Why first |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `model/Thresholds`, enums, records | Pure values, no dependencies |
| 2 | `routing/Topology`, `Route`, `TopologyRouter` | Needed by DataCenter.migrateOne |
| 3 | `model/DataCenter`, `EventLog` | Core ADTs with checkRep |
| 4 | `Nexus.g4`, `dsl/*` | Parser and interpreter |
| 5 | `agents/*` | Agents and safety layer |
| 6 | `sim/*` | Engine and fault injection |
| 7 | `web/*`, `NexusApp` | HTTP API and entry point |
| 8 | `resources/web/*` | Dashboard |
| 9 | `test/*` | Written from the partitions in Document 10 (test-first: before step 3–6 code) |

## Tree
```
nexus/
├── pom.xml.md, run.bat.md, run.sh.md, README.md.md
└── src/
    ├── main/antlr4/com/nexus/dsl/Nexus.g4.md
    ├── main/java/com/nexus/
    │   ├── NexusApp.java.md
    │   ├── model/    (19 files)
    │   ├── routing/  (3 files)
    │   ├── dsl/      (10 files)
    │   ├── agents/   (11 files)
    │   ├── sim/      (4 files)
    │   └── web/      (3 files)
    ├── main/resources/web/  index.html.md, css/style.css.md, js/app.js.md, js/scene.js.md, js/charts.js.md
    └── test/java/com/nexus/ (8 test classes)
```
